# [FABLE-5] sq-hmd7l.29 — Geographica real-world micro SPATIAL-SELECTION query
# "QUERY 15 - GeoNames_Point_Distance" (micro_selections.lst, geographica2.di.uoa.gr), pinned for
# scripts/bench/geo-same-box.sh (the GEO_GEOGRAPHICA=1 family; corpus recipe
# bench/geo/geographica.sh). TRANSLATIONS vs upstream (see bench/geo/README.md):
#   * GRAPH <http://geographica.di.uoa.gr/dataset/...> wrapper dropped — both
#     engines load the merged slice into the default graph; the per-dataset
#     predicate IRIs keep LGD/GeoNames distinguishable.
#   * COUNT-wrapped (counts-not-coordinates): only the result-set SIZE is
#     cross-checked between engines before any timing is trusted.
#   * upstream FILTER kept VERBATIM (standard geof:distance + uom:metre form);
#   *   sparq evaluates it as great-circle metres on the GRS80 mean sphere.
#   * jena-geosparql 5.4.0 CANNOT execute this form (planar SRS-native-unit
#   *   distance + degree->metre UnitsConversionException, root-caused in
#   *   research/gap-geo-2026-07.md §6d) -> the harness uses the pinned
#   *   q15_distance_geonames_point.jena.rq spatialF:nearby rendering there.
# Oracle: COUNT must equal expected-geographica.tsv before timing is trusted.
PREFIX geo:  <http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#>
PREFIX geof: <http://www.opengis.net/def/function/geosparql/>
PREFIX uom:  <http://www.opengis.net/def/uom/OGC/1.0/>
SELECT (COUNT(?s1) AS ?n) WHERE {
  ?s1 <http://www.geonames.org/ontology#asWKT> ?o1 .
  FILTER(geof:distance(?o1, "POINT(23.71622 37.97945)"^^geo:wktLiteral, uom:metre) <= 3000)
}
